<Base title="Writing — Matthew McMahon" description="The McLetter, plus two books in progress: Project M and the novel.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Writing</p>
    <h1>The words come first.</h1>
    <p>
      Everything I make starts as something I'm trying to work out on the page. The essays live in
      <a href="https://matthewmcmahon.beehiiv.com" style="color:var(--gold)">the McLetter</a> — a weekly
      letter on sound money, self-mastery, and building a life you actually own.
    </p>

    <h2>Project M</h2>
    <p>
      A nonfiction detective story. The biggest heist in history has already happened — the purchasing
      power of every person on earth, taken slowly, over generations. I walk you through the crime scene,
      lay out the evidence, and let you reach the verdict. One question runs through it: how did broken
      money break everything else — and what do we build now that we can see it?
    </p>

    <h2>The Novel</h2>
    <p>
      A kids' fantasy where sound money is the magic. Written so a kid learns what money really is before
      the world teaches them the opposite. The legacy play — plant the seed early.
    </p>

    <p style="color:var(--ink-faint)">The full archive is on its way here.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
